<script>
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';
  import { groupByCause, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';

  // The ticket filed for each cause.
  const TICKETS = {
    parser: 'https://github.com/apoganas/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/apoganas/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
  };

  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const groups = groupByCause(merged, tenantOf);
</script>

#4471 was merged on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Read by cause, it is not one issue. It holds two problems, so it now has two tickets.

## Tickets

<ul>
{#each groups as g (g.cause)}
  <li><code>{g.cause}</code> — <strong>{g.reports.length}</strong> reports — <a href={TICKETS[g.cause]}>ticket</a></li>
{/each}
</ul>

## The desk's own check

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changed

- One ticket per cause, each carrying the number of reports it covers.
- #4471 stays the `parser` ticket and keeps its reports.
- The `hint` reports are not this ticket's; they have their own now.

